From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sun, 29 Nov 2026 05:23:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Tests: the 3-D split's seam gate must test the cell
 star's closure

The parallel test builds the partition by hand (the patch's cell star on
rank 0, every other cell above it), so no fault facet point is shared while
the star's outer vertices are: the gap between split_fault's facet-only
gate and split_along_label_3d's refusal. It asserts the gate says touch on
every rank and split_fault succeeds. On the base it fails: the gate says no
touch and every rank refuses with 'cell star touches the partition seam'.
The serial test pins the shared helper the fix introduces on hand-marked
shared points.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
